WEBVTT

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:20.570
I guess I should have kept
looking in the city after all.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:26.440
No, in the city there's a high likelihood
they'd be picked up by kids,

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:29.320
and above all, they're easy to find there.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.690
Ooh, a nice wide-open space.
It should be easy to search here.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.570
Hey.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.820
What are you doing?

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.570
Uh, I'm just a--

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.570
Liar.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.690
You're a gatherer too, aren't you?

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:07.900
Well, this is my turf.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.650
I'll give you a choice.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:18.650
Die now... Or help me find the coins.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.690
I'll pass on both!

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.400
What should I do?

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:15.190
What's the right move here? I don't know!

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:20.280
There's no information to go on!

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.530
"Three hours earlier"

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.530
"Keep Out"
"Suspicious persons will be
reported to the police immediately"

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:31.440
Well, do you smell any humans?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.860
No. I don't think there's anyone around here.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.360
No surprise, huh?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.030
There aren't any trails
this deep in the mountains--

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.860
I don't think we'll find any people
out picking wildflowers!

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.480
In other words, if we run into anyone out here,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.900
it's safe to assume they're a monster.

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:01.610
What'll you do if we actually run into one?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:04.780
Honestly, it depends on what they do.

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:09.570
Ideally, we'd see them
before they see us and attack--

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:14.440
We can't do that!
We won't know if they're good or evil!

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:17.230
I thought you'd say that!

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:23.570
Although we won't last long
if we fight every person we meet.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:28.280
Plus, what we really need now is information.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:33.820
The alien told us we could
find lots of coins here,

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:35.610
but in a big area like this,

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:39.150
we're not going to find anything
just looking around randomly.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.400
We need to know exactly
where the other coins were found

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.940
and how many other monsters
or "gatherers" there are here.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:56.980
Who are the strongest ones?
Where are they and what are they doing?

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.360
We don't know anything.

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:09.230
If we find someone,
you should transform right away.

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:13.940
We'll probably find them before they find us...

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:16.900
Since you have that powerful nose.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:22.400
Are you sure I should transform?
What if they're just a normal person?

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.610
Dumbass. Remember?
Only monsters will come up here.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.860
It's the opposite of the town.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:35.320
Up here, we need to hide our real faces.

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:40.070
If we encounter someone bad
and they see who we are,

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:44.320
our normal lives will be in danger.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.860
They could threaten
to tell our school or our family,

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:53.110
or worse yet, our friends and family
could get caught up in the fight.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:59.610
Of course, facing them in
your monster form will put them on guard.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.900
Isn't it fascinating, though?

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.030
Huh?

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:07.360
Two monsters that don't know
each other's background, personality,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.730
or abilities, clashing with each other
in the middle of the mountains?

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.280
I wonder what'll happen.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.690
Clair, wait!

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.940
Don't go that way!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:33.280
Someone is there.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.360
Are they nearby?

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:37.570
I don't know.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:41.030
But it seems like they're not that close...

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:42.780
Maybe 200 meters off.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:47.150
Good. I have time to take off my clothes.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.320
Hurry up and transform.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:51.780
No way! Clair!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.110
We'll make the first move.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:00.360
We could avoid danger
and steadily gather up coins.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.940
That might seem like the
right approach at first glance.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.940
But it's not.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.530
While you're taking your time,

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:13.860
someone else could gather
all the coins and gain their power.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:20.570
If you're afraid of taking a risk,
you'll be too slow.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.230
In this world...

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.030
The right approach is to meet the risk head on.

00:07:34.030 --> 00:07:36.110
It's big.

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:39.320
Way bigger than me.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:45.440
And what's with those hands?
If it attacks me with those...

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:55.440
This is the first time
an enemy has approached me.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:59.400
Enemy?

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:03.860
I've felt the presence of
gatherers many times before,

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:08.530
but as soon as they see me, they run.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:14.150
I'm not your enemy. I just want to talk to you.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.820
Your voice... You're a girl.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.780
I see. Too bad.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:23.780
Well, I guess I shouldn't expect too much.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.610
Are you alone, too?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:28.820
How clever! She's making him
think there's only one person here.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.400
You want to talk about the coins, right?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:35.900
Sorry, but I don't know much about them.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:39.280
Same here. I was hoping we could help each--

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:42.980
I did not come her to look for coins.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:49.900
I wanted strength,
and this is what I got from the alien.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:57.440
But when I used it on normal people,
they were nothing.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:00.320
I couldn't get a feel for
my new strength at all.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:04.780
I want to know how strong I am.

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:11.690
The alien told me I could meet
other "gatherers" here.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.150
Honestly, I'm not excited about fighting a girl,

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.440
but I can't move forward without sacrifice.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.940
I'm sorry, but we must fight.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:24.980
I might have made a mistake here.

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.530
Shuichi, you idiot.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.820
Excellent.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:46.690
A normal human would have
been killed instantly by that strike.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:52.360
But I withstood it.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.860
That answers one question.

00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:57.570
He's so strong...

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:02.110
No... We'll be crushed...

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:05.980
Shuichi. That's enough.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:08.980
I'll take care of this.

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:13.230
Clair!

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:27.730
That was a solid strike! I could feel it!

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:44.530
We're in trouble.
This guy might be out of our league.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:50.400
I used the first monster we fought as
a standard to predict others' strength.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:55.230
But if everyone out here is like this guy...

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.070
Like her...

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:00.360
Clair...

00:11:00.360 --> 00:11:05.690
We can't die now...

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:10.110
Isn't that enough? I think we know now--

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:13.360
You're much stronger than me.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:17.940
But I didn't come here to fight you.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:22.150
The coins, huh? What do
you want them for, anyway?

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:25.070
Nothing, really.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:29.650
But if that kind of power ends up
in the hands of someone dangerous,

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.280
there's no telling what they'll use it for.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.530
That's why I want to share
as much information as possible--

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:36.280
I see.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:40.150
Well then, how can you prove
that you are not someone dangerous?

00:11:41.480 --> 00:11:46.730
Everyone searching for the coins,
everyone that seeks power thinks that way.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.900
They think everyone else is an enemy.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:52.440
That's how this place works.

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:55.900
That's why I came here.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.780
Too bad.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.860
I thought we could be friends.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.440
You good, Shuichi?

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:11.030
Yeah. I'm ready for this.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:16.190
I knew there would be fights
we couldn't avoid here...

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.360
And when they come, I won't hesitate!

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.030
That answers another question.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:31.900
My body can withstand bullets.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:35.480
Although it did pierce one of my arms...

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:40.070
That isn't a normal gun, is it?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:44.650
I was able to predict, to some degree,
where you'd aim, which allowed me to react.

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:47.150
Even if I was slightly off.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:54.360
I was confident that you would aim to kill.
Allow me to thank you.

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:59.360
My name is Tadanori Sanbe.
I'm a sophomore at Yamakita University.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:02.610
You're revealing your identity?

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:05.690
This is my way of saying thank you.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:10.690
You fought with your life, to take mine.
You deserve thanks.

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:14.030
Now it's my turn.

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:18.650
I always desired strength
and learned various martial arts.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:23.730
But those methods were
created by humans, for humans.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.320
They don't quite fit this form.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:30.360
What the hell is that stance?

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:34.480
I came up with my own martial art form.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.320
I've yet to perfect it--it's not the prettiest.

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:39.110
Would you like to see it?

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.780
Oh...

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.030
Shit!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.320
Hmm, it still needs work.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:02.480
Power alone is not enough.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:08.860
To use it in a real fight,
I must be accurate as well.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:12.480
Another question answered.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:16.190
Still, I did feel decent impact.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:20.070
She shouldn't be able to get far.

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:23.610
Stop hiding!

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:26.480
Our fight is not over yet!

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:32.150
You leave me no choice.

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:36.190
This might get a bit messy.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.690
What are you doing?

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:57.230
Seriously? You want to see who's stronger?

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:59.940
Are you screwing with me?

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:03.400
You should know by now--
my raw strength is beyond yours!

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:08.030
Or are you now afraid of
putting your life on the line?

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:12.530
You've disappointed me.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:17.730
Die.

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:19.400
You first.

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.900
Who the hell is that?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.980
Where did you come from?

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.440
You lose.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.730
Was a friend of yours hiding?

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:38.690
No, this is the same voice I heard before.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:42.690
So who is this one?

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.780
Wonderful.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:53.440
The tables have completely turned on me,
and I don't even know how.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:59.070
So this is what it means
to put your life on the line.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.980
You're stronger than I thought.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:10.480
I doubt I can shake you off in time...

00:16:10.480 --> 00:16:13.610
Is she controlling this thing?

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:18.230
You lose. Admit it.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.900
I don't want to kill anyone!

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:21.900
Shuichi!

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:24.940
No, there are two of them!

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:28.780
This one must be a gatherer that transformed.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:33.030
So who is she?

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:34.610
Can I ask you a question?

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:36.480
No!

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:41.440
If that girl is a normal human...

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:44.610
That gun was powerful enough to pierce my arm.

00:16:44.610 --> 00:16:47.400
If she fires it...

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.530
Do you realize it?

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:57.110
I see.

00:17:03.230 --> 00:17:05.440
All right then.

00:17:05.900 --> 00:17:07.980
I lose.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.280
Shuichi!

00:17:14.190 --> 00:17:16.360
No, Clair!

00:17:16.360 --> 00:17:20.860
I didn't think he'd transform back like that!

00:17:20.860 --> 00:17:27.150
Don't worry about it.
It's his fault for doing something so dumb.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:30.110
You're exactly right.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:33.360
We put our lives on the line.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:36.230
And I lost.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:39.440
Kill me.

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.570
You really are dumb.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:49.730
We gain nothing by killing you.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:55.610
And yet we had to "put our lives
on the line" for your stupid fight.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:59.400
How are you going to make this up to us?

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:00.940
Clair...

00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:05.690
I'm sorry.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.940
Give me your phone.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.230
I don't have one.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.860
You're lying!

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.860
It's true.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.730
Why?

00:18:15.730 --> 00:18:18.780
It's not manly!

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:27.230
Lady... Don't you think it's time
you put some clothes on?

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:30.400
I can't! I left them somewhere back there.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:35.190
If you don't have a phone,
give me your address and phone number.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.980
Ooh, nice!

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:44.730
Let me have it, too! And you two, give me yours.

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.280
Shuichi?!

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.650
I didn't notice!

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:52.320
He was downwind from us,
so I didn't catch his scent!

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:55.110
Don't try to run, now.
I got some lovely pictures of your faces.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:19:02.440
Even if you run back to town, I'll find you.

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:08.480
Me and my friends are gonna
make you feel real special, girl.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:15.730
You can't go making a ruckus
like that in these mountains...

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:20.940
Or some dangerous type like me
is going to find you.

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:25.280
From now on, you're my slaves.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.070
I'm thankful...

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:35.530
You're clearly low-life scum...

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.650
Huh?

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:44.030
...so I'll have no second
thoughts about killing you.

00:19:48.900 --> 00:19:50.860
He killed...

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:04.780
Ah, that's great.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:11.320
You're so powerful--I thought
all the monsters were like you.

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:14.030
It looks like that's not the case!

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.820
So... What should I do?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:26.650
You've got to help us look for coins, of course!

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:31.650
I'm sure you'll have plenty
of chances to test your strength.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.690
I look forward to it.

00:20:35.690 --> 00:20:39.280
You can wait till you heal, if you want.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:41.820
You broke some ribs, didn't you?

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.320
Huh?

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:47.570
Uh... Are you okay?

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:54.610
You gave me this, didn't you?

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.150
Thank you.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:02.820
What's your relationship with that girl?

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:09.400
I turn into the costume thing,
and she gets inside and fights.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:18.280
Yeah... I didn't do anything this time, either.

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:24.230
Was splitting up her idea?

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:25.070
Huh?

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.940
No, it wasn't.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:32.650
That idiot said he'd be bait,
and I could run away.

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:32.650
Idiot?!

00:21:32.650 --> 00:21:36.190
That's why I set it up that way.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.440
I hated that plan though.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:43.400
If I'm going to die, I want to die with Shuichi.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.730
I see.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:50.320
Shuichi, you're a real man.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:57.150
All right. I'll join you.

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:59.730
You have my life.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:06.400
Great! We should probably go back
before this guy's friends come.

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:10.610
I just found our next prey, too.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:47.030
"Episode 6: Gatherers"
